@startuml
title Strijder repeated peripheral branch - conceptual connectivity
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "VPERIPH_n\nSelected regulated input rail" as RAIL
rectangle "C201\nLocal input decoupling" as CIN
rectangle "U201\nHigh-side protection / eFuse\nCurrent limit + short shutdown + ramp\nReverse blocking if required" as SW
rectangle "R201 / C203\nILIM / fault timer / ramp networks\nSelected controller circuit TBD" as CFG
rectangle "C202 / D201\nOutput decoupling / connector clamp" as OUT
rectangle "J201\nSupply contact(s): allocation TBD\nReturn contact(s): allocation TBD" as CONN
rectangle "Harness + peripheral\nLoad voltage / steady / inrush TBD" as LOAD
rectangle "U105 supervisor\nHardware-safe default enables\nVoltage and current telemetry" as MCU
rectangle "PWR_RTN\nSized intentional return path" as RTN
rectangle "CHASSIS\nApproved shield termination" as CHASSIS

RAIL --> SW : input
RAIL --> CIN : shunt tap
CIN -- RTN
CFG ..> SW : controller-specific setup
SW --> CONN : VBR_n
SW --> OUT : VBR_n shunt tap
OUT -- RTN
CONN --> LOAD : fused/protected supply path
LOAD --> CONN : dedicated return conductor(s)
CONN --> RTN : branch return current
MCU ..> SW : EN_n
SW ..> MCU : FAULT_n / IMON_n / PG_n
CONN ..> MCU : protected VBR_n sense
CONN .. CHASSIS : shield bond strategy TBD

note right of SW
  Functional example: TPS25982 family on a
  compatible protected rail, not a selected
  automotive raw-battery interface.
  Confirm exact reverse-blocking behavior.
end note
note right of CONN
  Parallel contacts do not guarantee equal current.
  Total-current protection may miss overload
  of a single surviving contact.
  Connector pin numbers remain unassigned.
end note
note bottom of LOAD
  Inductive actuators need dedicated driver and clamp analysis.
  Power-over-coax requires separate injection/link design.
  Warning-light lamp loads are not this generic peripheral branch.
end note
legend bottom
  CONCEPTUAL / NOT FOR FABRICATION
  All component values, trip limits and layout details TBD.
  Dotted lines indicate sensing/control/shield intent, not power.
endlegend
@enduml
